---
import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
---

<LegalPage
	title="Privacy Notice"
	description="How Litepod Studio handles personal information.">
	<p>
		Litepod Studio respects your privacy. This notice explains how we handle
		personal information when you visit Litepod or use Litepod Cloud.
	</p>
	<h2>Information we collect</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			Information you provide when you contact us, create an account, or request
			support.
		</li>
		<li>
			Technical and usage information, such as device, browser, pages visited,
			and interactions with the website.
		</li>
		<li>
			Security information about your Litepod Cloud account: sign-ins, failed
			sign-in attempts and account security changes, with the IP address,
			browser, time, and an approximate location (country, city and network
			provider) derived from the IP address.
		</li>
		<li>
			Payment and purchase information handled by Paddle for paid Litepod Cloud
			services.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<h2>How we use it</h2>
	<p>
		We use this information to provide and secure Litepod, process purchases,
		support users, understand website performance, and meet legal obligations.
		We use sign-in security information only to protect accounts, for example to
		detect a sign-in from a new country or from places too far apart in too
		little time. Only the Litepod administration team can see it.
		We do not sell personal information.
	</p>
	<h2>Analytics and local storage</h2>
	<p>
		This website uses Umami analytics and session recording to understand how
		visitors use the site. Your browser also stores your selected light or dark
		theme locally. You can limit analytics through your browser settings or
		privacy tools.
	</p>
	<h2>Sharing and retention</h2>
	<p>
		We share information only with service providers that help us operate
		Litepod, including Paddle for payments, Umami for analytics, and ip.guide (with
		ipwho.is as a fallback), which receives only the IP address of a sign-in to
		look up its approximate location, or when
		required by law. We retain information only as long as needed for these
		purposes, including legal and accounting requirements.
	</p>
	<h2>Your choices</h2>
	<p>
		You may request access, correction, deletion, or other privacy assistance by
		emailing{" "}<a href="mailto:info@litepod.sh">info@litepod.sh</a>. We may
		need to verify your request and may retain information where the law permits
		or requires it.
	</p>
	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		For privacy questions, contact Litepod Studio at
		{" "}<a href="mailto:info@litepod.sh">info@litepod.sh</a>.
	</p>
</LegalPage>
